{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1782556331,"nonce":"NYySxWjVmVxI9ldhrpntLCj6Btc=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABG5hPFg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/338","origin":"github"},"title":"Add time-sync diagnostics (gabby ↔ mercat ↔ M3) — detect clock-skew faults live","message":"## Problem\n\nA ~6 s time-sync fault on the M3 went **undetected for days**. Per-day analysis of the gabby bags shows the M3 detection timestamps were healthy (~0.05 s behind receive time) through **June 23**, then jumped to a rock-steady **+6.03 s** starting **June 24** and stayed there (24/25/26):\n\n| Date | M3 stamp − receive | | Date | M3 stamp − receive |\n|------|------:|---|------|------:|\n| Jun 12 | +0.08 s | | Jun 22 | +0.07 s |\n| Jun 15 | +0.05 s | | Jun 23 | +0.04 s |\n| Jun 16 | +0.04 s | | **Jun 24** | **+6.03 s** |\n| Jun 17 | +0.07 s | | Jun 25 | +6.04 s |\n| Jun 18 | +0.04 s | | Jun 26 | +6.04 s |\n| Jun 19 | +0.04 s | | | |\n\nDuring the bad window every *other* clock on the boat (nav/TF, GPS, IMU, SBG, Garmin sidescan) agreed with receive time to **\u003c 2 ms** — the M3 was the lone outlier. A 6 s offset smears bathy georef by **~9 m** at survey speed. Nothing flagged it; it was only found by offline bag forensics after the fact.\n\nThere are at least three clocks in play and no diagnostic watching any of them:\n- **gabby** (autonomy host — nav, TF, bag recording)\n- **mercat** (hydro-payload host — runs the M3/SBG/SVS, see #76)\n- the **M3 head's own clock** (PPS-disciplined rate; absolute time-of-day from ZDA)\n\nThe +6 s signature (stable offset, no drift) is consistent with PPS disciplining the *rate* while the head's absolute time-of-day is set wrong — i.e. a ZDA/time-of-day delivery problem, plausibly a gabby↔mercat skew or the ZDA going to the wrong place. The regression is a discrete step on the night of Jun 23 → 24.\n\n## Ask\n\nAdd diagnostics that **detect time-sync issues across gabby, mercat, and the M3 data** and publish to `/diagnostics` (so they surface live in the operator HUD and land in bags), with WARN/ERROR thresholds that would have caught this on Jun 24.\n\n### Proposed checks\n\n1. **Host ↔ host clock offset (gabby ↔ mercat).** Monitor chrony/NTP/PPS sync state and the measured offset between hosts. WARN above a small threshold (e.g. 50 ms), ERROR above ~0.5 s. (Relates to chrony hygiene in #129.)\n2. **M3 datagram-time vs arrival-time skew.** Compare the M3 detection `header.stamp` (datagram clock, via `kongsberg_em_bridge`) against ROS receive time. A stable offset beyond ~0.5 s = ERROR. This is the check that directly catches the +6 s. Note: `kongsberg_em_bridge`'s `em_time_to_unix` currently only rejects *grossly* corrupt dates — a plausible-but-wrong time (like this one) passes straight through with no warning. A sanity check belongs either in the bridge or this monitor.\n3. **Cross-sensor stamp coherence (optional).** Compare M3 stamp drift vs a trusted reference (GPS/SBG) so a single number captures \"is the bathy timestamp trustworthy right now.\"\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- A node (e.g. a `time_sync_monitor`, mirroring the existing `teltonika_monitor`/`mikrotik_monitor` pattern in `ros2_network_monitor`) publishes per-check `diagnostic_msgs` status.\n- Replaying a Jun 24–26 bag (or injecting a 6 s skew) produces an ERROR; a healthy Jun 18 bag stays OK.\n- Wired into the boat via `network_monitor_boat_launch.py` and visible in the operator diagnostics.\n\n## Related / context\n\n- #337 (`rolker/unh_echoboats_project11`) — FCU 3D-gyro RCA. A **separate** fault (broke Jun 18 → 19, not the same event), but found in the same investigation; both degrade bathy.\n- #129 — chrony/NTP host config hygiene (the host side of check 1).\n- #76 — M3/SBG/SVS payload integration on mercat (why gabby↔mercat skew matters).\n- Implementation of the reusable monitor node may live in `rolker/ros2_network_monitor` alongside the existing monitors; this issue owns the deployment requirement and wiring.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}